WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:01.900
- No, but speaking of, you
have your own new show.

00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:02.920
You have your new podcast, right?

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:04.270
- I do, yeah, yeah.

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:05.637
- [Kelly] Tell everybody what it's about.

00:00:05.637 --> 00:00:07.887
(applause)

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:11.970
I mean, in the last
few years of my career,

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:16.350
I really realized how much
I loved inspiring people,

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:19.040
and I had this cool
platform where just being

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:20.310
out there was enough.

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:23.590
And so, after racing, I
thought the one thing that

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:26.230
I really want to keep
doing is doing that --

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:29.150
giving people inspiration,
making sure that

00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:30.700
they understand that they can do anything,

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:34.070
and setting big goals and digging deeper

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:36.700
into themselves to grow and so,

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:39.820
this show came up as an
idea between a group of us

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:41.870
and I was like, "I think this is perfect."

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:43.590
So, I mean, it's so much fun.

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:44.440
Look, when you
- [Kelly] I want to be on it!

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:45.540
- get interviewed,

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:47.270
you don't learn crap,
because you just talk

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:48.310
about yourself.

00:00:48.310 --> 00:00:49.143
- Exactly!

00:00:49.143 --> 00:00:50.690
It's much harder to flip it.

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:54.150
- But when you do interview
people, you learn a ton!

00:00:54.150 --> 00:00:56.260
Right, like, I'm sure you've
been meeting so many --

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:58.010
even more people than you already met.

00:00:58.010 --> 00:00:59.740
- Yes, and actually,
it's like my first time,

00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:01.770
like, in my life that I've
actually just shut up.

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:03.436
Like...
- [Danica] Oh, by the way...

00:01:03.436 --> 00:01:06.150
- Which is working out! It
turns out I like listening!

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:07.130
- Yeah.

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:08.481
- I didn't know this about myself.

00:01:08.481 --> 00:01:10.731
(applause)

00:01:12.017 --> 00:01:14.850
- I sympathize, as I've said that one

00:01:14.850 --> 00:01:17.680
of the hardest things for
me to do is to just shut up

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:19.880
and listen, and it's
almost like a discipline,

00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:22.080
an exercise for me, in growth.

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:24.100
So, doing the show is really good,

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:26.620
and the shows are usually between, gosh,

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:27.910
an hour to an hour-and-a-half?

00:01:27.910 --> 00:01:29.940
So, that's a lot of listening.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:30.773
- Yeah, but,
(audience laughter)

00:01:30.773 --> 00:01:31.920
at the same time, though, I do feel like

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:33.630
it takes a minute to really invest,

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:35.080
and you're wanting to do
something that's powerful

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:36.490
and inspiring -- it takes a minute,

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:37.810
that's not, like, a five-minute thing.

00:01:37.810 --> 00:01:38.650
That's cool.

00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:39.483
- It takes a while.

00:01:39.483 --> 00:01:41.181
So, we're gonna be here a while?

00:01:41.181 --> 00:01:42.120
(laughter)

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:44.810
- I'm gonna break down that
barrier in eight minutes!

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:46.580
- [Danica] Oh, no!
- I've been challenged!

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:47.710
- Yeah, well, that's the other thing,

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:50.970
is I'm very, very
vulnerable and very honest

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:52.170
and if somebody asks me a question,

00:01:52.170 --> 00:01:53.660
I will answer it.

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:56.729
And, it's probably why so many
people love you, you know.

00:01:56.729 --> 00:01:57.985
- I think that's why
(audience applause)

00:01:57.985 --> 00:02:00.463
so many people look up to you.

00:02:00.463 --> 00:02:02.550
What I do want to know is,
are you having fun, because...

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:03.710
Is retiring good?

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:05.650
- [Danica] Yeah, I mean,
like, I do feel like

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:07.817
I'm growing so much,
but when people ask me,

00:02:07.817 --> 00:02:09.150
"You're retired -- how is it?"

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:12.417
And I'm like, "I mean, vacations...?

00:02:12.417 --> 00:02:14.305
"Farmer's markets...?"
(audience applause)

00:02:14.305 --> 00:02:15.792
- Yes.

00:02:15.792 --> 00:02:19.390
- I mean, like, I can lean
into somethin' like that!

00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:20.223
- [Kelly] I envy...

00:02:20.223 --> 00:02:21.750
- So, no, it's not just that, but I mean,

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:24.610
I have a wine named 'Somnium,'
so I've been able to do

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:25.550
more stuff for that.
- [Kelly] Whaaat?

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:27.244
- Yeah, I do speaking engagements
and all kinds of stuff.

00:02:27.244 --> 00:02:28.077
- You're very motivated.

00:02:28.077 --> 00:02:29.510
- But a lot of vacations.

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:30.440
- [Kelly] I love that.

00:02:30.440 --> 00:02:31.273
- Yup. Yup.

00:02:31.273 --> 00:02:33.120
- Everybody's gettin'
a bottle of wine, guys!

00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:38.120
- [Danica] Yes!
(audience cheering)

00:02:38.176 --> 00:02:40.860
- I'm -- this is the first season!

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.048
This ain't Oprah, y'all!

00:02:42.048 --> 00:02:43.810
- Oh, it's no, okay!

00:02:43.810 --> 00:02:45.623
I'm sorry, Kelly, I overstepped!

00:02:45.623 --> 00:02:46.456
(audience laughing)
I got excited.

00:02:46.456 --> 00:02:47.620
- You gotta wait 'til the second season!

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:48.460
I gotta make sure people like this!

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:51.030
- I was gonna give you one,
and then she just said, "No."

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:52.603
- Well, me, mmm'kay....

00:02:53.601 --> 00:02:54.470
- (laughing) I'm getting one,

00:02:54.470 --> 00:02:56.289
you're going to watch me drink it.

00:02:56.289 --> 00:02:58.090
(audience laughing) No, that's weird.

00:02:58.090 --> 00:03:00.430
No, but, I was, like,
asking drivers this, like,

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:01.820
you're driving your whole life, right?

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:03.120
But, what about your driver's test?

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:04.650
'Cause, I find that most
- Oh, yeah...

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:07.050
- I find that most of
y'all actually did horribly

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:08.180
on your driver's test.

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:10.144
- Nah, I was good.

00:03:10.144 --> 00:03:11.460
(audience laughing)
- You were good?

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:13.910
- Well, the teacher is
in the passenger's seat,

00:03:13.910 --> 00:03:15.840
and they have an extra
brake on their side.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:18.640
And I don't slow -- he was really nervous

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:20.010
and hovered over the brake a lot,

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:22.460
because I didn't slow down
because of brake lights,

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:24.310
I slowed down because of closing rates.

00:03:24.310 --> 00:03:26.250
So, until the car actually came back to me

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:28.630
from a distance perspective,
I didn't slow down,

00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:30.137
so I freaked him out all the time.

00:03:30.137 --> 00:03:30.970
(audience laughing)

00:03:30.970 --> 00:03:31.803
- You know what, though?

00:03:31.803 --> 00:03:32.636
It worked out. (laughs)

00:03:32.636 --> 00:03:34.210
- But, I was -- I think he's told stories

00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:35.043
about me afterwards.

00:03:35.043 --> 00:03:36.675
I think they were good, I don't know.

00:03:36.675 --> 00:03:37.937
(audience laughing)

00:03:37.937 --> 00:03:39.613
- [Kelly] Who cares?!
- Yeah, I got my license.

00:03:39.613 --> 00:03:40.872
- [Kelly] You have your own show!

00:03:40.872 --> 00:03:41.810
- [Danica] (laughs) Duh!

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:44.800
- Did you do well on your
driving tests, you two?

00:03:44.800 --> 00:03:46.190
- Uh, nahhhh...

00:03:46.190 --> 00:03:47.810
- I almost failed mine.

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:49.330
- You know, no, I did pretty good.

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:51.120
You know, my worst driving
experience was the first time

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:53.680
I tried to drive listening
to a book on tape.

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:54.513
You know?

00:03:54.513 --> 00:03:56.700
Because, I thought that
was a really good idea

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:57.617
and the person riding was, like,

00:03:57.617 --> 00:03:59.718
"Aw, man, I been asleep for 15 minutes,"

00:03:59.718 --> 00:04:01.384
and I was, like, "Me,
too!" (audience laughing)

00:04:01.384 --> 00:04:02.217
You know what I mean?

00:04:02.217 --> 00:04:05.217
(audience applause)

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:08.410
- Do you --
- Like, this is such

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:10.297
a bad idea to listening to a book on tape.

00:04:10.297 --> 00:04:12.453
- [Kelly] I'm just kidding,
you're safe. You're safe!

00:04:12.453 --> 00:04:13.820
Mindy, you do stunt work;

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:15.830
have you ever done any with, like, cars?

00:04:15.830 --> 00:04:18.040
- I hire people to do precision driving,

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:19.240
but for the most part,

00:04:19.240 --> 00:04:20.187
- [Kelly] I love that,
- I actually jump

00:04:20.187 --> 00:04:21.020
out of the way.

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:21.853
- You just led with,

00:04:21.853 --> 00:04:22.865
"I hire them (finger
snaps) to do it." (laughs)

00:04:22.865 --> 00:04:23.698
(audience cheering and applause)

00:04:23.698 --> 00:04:24.531
- Boss!

00:04:24.531 --> 00:04:25.364
- Amazing!

00:04:25.364 --> 00:04:26.893
(audience applause)
That's cool!

